    "Description": "OpenSSH is an SSH protocol implementation supported by a number of Linux, UNIX, and similar operating systems. It includes the core files necessary for both the OpenSSH client and server.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* openssh: OpenSSH: sftp client allows attacker to control downloaded file location (CVE-2026-59995)\n\n* openssh: OpenSSH sshd: Security bypass due to incorrect handling of forwarding and tunneling options (CVE-2026-59999)\n\n* openssh: OpenSSH: Information disclosure and data corruption via use-after-free in ssh client (CVE-2026-73282)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* Incomplete backport of CVE-2023-38408 in RHEL 8 openssh (JIRA:RHEL-234763)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
